{
 "name": "narrowtail6",
 "description": "Pinned 160 mm chassis; two 15:1 L-motor drives rotate opposed 42.93 mm cranks with locked rubber tyre feet. Continuous contact-driven stepping crosses rods without timed lifting. Gearbox upper ties are full-depth 6L shafts with stops on both outer bearing faces, replacing shallow bridging pins. Full-length inner and outer gearbox beams tied below gears with internally retained 4L shafts. Raised passive tail tyres arrest rearward pitching; laminated tail deck joins both rear bearing extensions. Gearbox base L-braces have multiple chassis pins 8,16,24 mm from the drive axle and two vertical frame pins. Rear/front rail extensions locked to central splice beams with three full-depth transverse pin stations. Four outboard feet use narrower 30.4 mm tyres moved 8 mm inward, with 5L foot shafts; four inner 43.2 mm tyres retain full reach.",
 "part_set": "inventory",
 "chassis": "rail_l",
 "motor": "motor_r",
